# 14. Class Imbalance 🔥

Imagine a fraud dataset:

```text
Normal transactions = 99,000
Fraud transactions  = 1,000
```

That's:

```text
Normal → 99%
Fraud  → 1%
```

A model predicting everything as normal gets:

$$
99\%
$$

accuracy.

Sounds good.

But it detects:

$$
0
$$

fraud cases.

Therefore:

> **EDA can reveal class imbalance before you make the mistake of relying on accuracy.**

